    {
      "id": "ILT-02",
      "title": "The triangular span and the cost of one extra row",
      "chapter": "lifts",
      "anchor": "lifts-inert-length-derivation",
      "statement": "Mixed middle rows (0,C⁻¹,Vgb) produce a last-coordinate generator y=ϖ^{−α−t}. Use the first standard row when a≥0 and the first row of the cell matrix when a<0 to form the triangular block matrix P. The full lattice is generated by the rows of P and one additional row with coordinates ρ=(0,ϖ^α rC,ϖ^α(c−r·CVgb)/y). Since −v(det P)=|a|+h+t, replacing a row at the largest denominator exponent t′=max(t,S−2α−t) computes the full length.",
      "dependencies": [
        "IDU-01"
      ],
      "equations": [
        "lifts-inert-length-extra"
      ],
